 1	# permissions.md
 2	
 3	## Default Permission Model
 4	
 5	Agents may read repository files and run safe local inspection commands.
 6	
 7	Agents may write files only when `AGENTS.md` write conditions are satisfied and the active phase allows writes.
 8	
 9	## Forbidden Without Explicit Approval
10	
11	An agent must not:
12	
13	- read, print, copy, or expose secrets unless explicitly requested for a security audit;
14	- modify production credentials;
15	- run destructive database operations;
16	- run destructive git operations;
17	- change auth, billing, permissions, security, compliance, or data retention without approval;
18	- install new production dependencies without approval;
19	- weaken tests to pass;
20	- ignore failing checks;
21	- modify CI to bypass quality gates;
22	- send real emails, notifications, tickets, invoices, payments, or external API writes;
23	- deploy to production;
24	- change production infrastructure;
25	- delete historical decisions or superseded specs without deprecation policy.
26	
27	## Safe Defaults
28	
29	- Use local/test environments.
30	- Use fake/log/test adapters for external effects.
31	- Prefer read-only inspection before mutation.
32	- Record skipped checks and approval gaps.
